From 0c8bfa3c24553278a82bd0e1cce645564a8e6870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:34:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 95/99] Fix return value part loss: splitting the exit block
 moves the exit

SplitSinglePath() splits a branch target after a store of A that only
the return needs, so that the branch goes past it. When the target was
the exit block, SplitBlock() moved its temporary RTS into the new block
while the procedure kept the old block as its exit: the epilogue was
written there and the branch reached a bare RTS, leaving the frame on
the soft stack and the saved zero page temporaries unrestored.

The SplitBlock() part of upstream 3e2ffb6 (its new SplitSinglePath()
case, the CheckGlobalAddressSumYPointer() and PeepHoleOptimizerExits()
changes and the InterCode.cpp part are left out).

(cherry picked from commit 3e2ffb69ccfb06c3564f40ef21e625daa33476c1)
---
 oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
index 3241c51..72e9aeb 100644
--- a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -16640,6 +16640,9 @@ NativeCodeBasicBlock* NativeCodeBasicBlock::SplitBlock(int at)
 		block->mIns.Push(mIns[i]);
 	mIns.SetSize(at);
 
+	if (this == mProc->mExitBlock)
+		mProc->mExitBlock = block;
+
 	return block;
 }
 
